        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "No provider's usage shape is known, so the record is twine's own and every usage value in the tests is a named double (brief \u00a72); nothing maps a provider onto it yet.",
            "A JSON number for cost_usd may be a rounded double of the exact value; the check decides on the exact Decimal, and the contract says so."
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Money is Decimal end to end (tomllib parse_float=Decimal, Decimal cap); only the JSON twin rounds to a double, so 0.1+0.2 against a 0.3 cap admits.",
            "A record whose served_sid equals its sid is malformed (writer and reader), since it would count twice in that session's spend so far.",
            "A session named only as a served_sid gets a totals row with calls 0, thinking 0 (not null).",
            "Totals price every record: an unpriced model anywhere makes totals not ok even with --sid; tokens still render, every cost null.",
            "The check ignores other sessions' unpriced history but refuses on any malformed line anywhere in the stream.",
            "The price file is validated whole; it is read by totals only when there is a record to price.",
            "No state directory resolvable is a refusal (no-state-dir); the working directory is never a fallback, and a relative XDG_STATE_HOME is ignored per the XDG spec.",
            "An empty --state-dir or --prices is a bad-argument refusal, never read as an absent flag (found by an independent review pass).",
            "Bad --cap/--input/--max-output values are a named bad-argument refusal (exit 1), not an argparse usage error; a missing flag stays argparse's exit 2.",
            "The writer fsyncs, creates the directory 0700 and the file 0600, and refuses to append onto a torn last line; the reader names a torn line.",
            "Every report carries one closed `refusal` set, and the check's `stop` is set only for cap-reached; an uncheckable cap has stop null (a stop key for it is proposed in notes.md)."
          ],
